{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_cluster_bootstrap", "label": "Cluster bootstrap phase", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Runs before Cluster.join so that at most one cluster comes out of a simultaneous start; gossip never repairs two clusters with the same name, each with its own leader, singletons and shard allocations.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_stableobservation", "label": "StableObservation", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Polls the seed provider and requires the returned set to be byte-identical for stableMarginMs before acting; a failed lookup is not an empty set and does not count as an observation, so a DNS outage can never be mistaken for 'I am alone'.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_deferred_self_election", "label": "Deferred self-election", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The lowest-addressed node still joins the others as seeds and only gets a deadline; addresses are handed out by the platform, so a later-starting node can sort first and immediate self-election would form a second cluster beside the running one.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_bootstrapcluster", "label": "bootstrapCluster()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_clusterbootstrapoptions", "label": "ClusterBootstrapOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_required_contact_points", "label": "requiredContactPoints", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The margin catches discovery that is slow; only a required count catches discovery that is stably wrong - a resolver that consistently returns two of three pods settles happily on the wrong set. The default of 1 exists so single-node development needs no configuration.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_stableobservationerror", "label": "StableObservationError", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "There is no degraded fallback to a direct join: joining anyway would be indistinguishable from the failure the phase prevents. A start that fails loudly is recoverable by a restart or an operator; a second cluster is not.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_cluster_bootstrap_wildcard_host_refusal", "label": "Wildcard advertised host is refused", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The election is ordered on this node's address, so 0.0.0.0 (a bind address) makes every node sort identically, believe it won and form its own cluster; the phase rejects it up front.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/cluster-bootstrap.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source":